Feature: Choosing and testing the guest link

  @AC-15 @TL-4
  Scenario Outline: Both channels pass one conformance suite on live VMs
    Given a second instance with guest link "<link>"
    And a lease of image "<image>" with the Tart guest agent installed
    When the conformance suite runs
    Then every case passes or is recorded as failing with its evidence
    And the report records round-trip time per operation for this link and image

    Examples:
      | link         | image      |
      | ssh-session  | macos26    |
      | ssh-session  | ubuntu2404 |
      | tart-session | macos26    |
      | tart-session | ubuntu2404 |

  @AC-16 @TL-2
  Scenario: The guest link is selected by configuration
    Given machine-service started with MACHINE_SERVICE_GUEST_LINK set to "ssh"
    Then every exec starts its own ssh process
    Given machine-service started with MACHINE_SERVICE_GUEST_LINK set to "ssh-session"
    Then execs share one guest session
    Given machine-service started with MACHINE_SERVICE_GUEST_LINK set to an unknown value
    Then machine-service refuses to start and names the accepted values

  @AC-17 @TL-1 @TL-2
  Scenario: Offline suites need no Tart, SSH or network
    When "cargo test --workspace" runs on a machine without Tart, sshd or network access
    Then every unit and component integration test of both links runs and passes

  @AC-18 @TL-4
  Scenario: Live tests leave the installed service alone
    Given the installed vm-service running on port 6240
    When the live suites run against a second instance on another port and state directory
    Then the installed service's process, state directory and leases are unchanged

Feature: Federation, rename and installation

  @AC-34 @TL-2 @TL-6
  Scenario: The CLI lists every machine from every instance
    Given the local instance and two instances that Consul lists as "machine-service"
    And one of those instances is stopped
    When the operator runs "machctl list"
    Then the list shows the local instance's machines first, then the reachable instance's machines
    And the stopped instance appears as "unreachable" with its error and its Consul health status
    And the local instance appears once even though Consul also lists it

  @AC-35 @TL-2
  Scenario: Old paths fail loudly after the coordinated switch
    Given the renamed service
    When a client sends GET /vms or POST /vms/<name>/exec
    Then the answer is HTTP 410 Gone and the error names the /machines path that replaces it
    And no operation runs
    When the operator runs "machctl list" and "machctl --help"
    Then the output matches machctl's golden help files
    And no "vmctl" link remains in "~/.local/bin" pointing into the old install folder

  @AC-36 @TL-2
  Scenario: An old variable name stops the daemon, and the installer rewrites it
    Given machine-service started with VM_SERVICE_PORT set to 6290
    Then it refuses to start and names VM_SERVICE_PORT and its replacement MACHINE_SERVICE_PORT
    Given an installed vm-service whose LaunchAgent sets VM_SERVICE_HOST and VM_SERVICE_GUEST_LINK
    When the operator runs "machine-service-install install"
    Then the new LaunchAgent sets MACHINE_SERVICE_HOST and MACHINE_SERVICE_GUEST_LINK to the same values
    And it sets no VM_SERVICE_* variable

  @AC-45 @TL-1 @TL-2
  Scenario: An old environment profile is refused with its fix
    Given a selected-environment profile at schemaVersion 1 with a vmctlPath field
    When the operator runs "machctl --environment <profile> environment --json"
    Then it fails and the error names machctlPath and schemaVersion 2
    And pilot-images' bootstrap and mcp-relay's environment loader refuse the same profile the same way
    Given the same profile at schemaVersion 2 with machctlPath naming the machctl executable
    Then the command prints the resolved profile and exports MACHCTL, and no VMCTL

  @AC-37 @TL-6
  Scenario: Each instance is registered in Consul with the tags it warrants
    Given the catalog description printed by "machine-service-install catalog-description" is placed on each Mac
    Then Consul lists "machine-service" on mac-mini-m4-pro with the tags vm and tart and without durable
    And Consul lists "machine-service" on mac-mini-m4-1 and mac-mini-m4-2 with the tag durable and without vm
    And Consul lists no "vm-service"

  @AC-38 @TL-6
  Scenario: An instance on a Mac without Tart offers only its durable machine
    Given a Mac with no Tart installed
    When the operator installs machine-service there with durable exposure on and without the virtual-machine helpers
    Then the installer succeeds
    And GET /health reports kinds ["durable"]
    And GET /machines lists the durable machine and no virtual machine offer
    And an acquisition with an image is refused with HTTP 400 naming the missing Tart

  @AC-39 @TL-1 @TL-2 @TL-4
  Scenario: Adding and removing an image line changes the list without a restart
    Given a running instance whose image repository has the lines "macos26" and "ubuntu2404"
    When the operator adds the line folder "linux-extra" with a valid line.conf
    Then GET /images and GET /machines list "linux-extra" on the next request, and the daemon's process ID is unchanged
    And an acquisition of image "linux-extra" succeeds
    When the operator removes the folder "ubuntu2404" while a lease of "ubuntu2404" is running
    Then the next GET /images no longer lists "ubuntu2404"
    And the running lease's heartbeat and release still succeed

  @AC-40 @TL-2 @TL-4
  Scenario: Editing a line and promoting a base take effect without a restart
    Given a running instance
    When the operator changes CPU from 6 to 4 in "images/macos26/line.conf"
    Then "machctl images-show macos26" reports a CPU default of 4
    Given a line whose base VM does not exist yet
    When the operator promotes its work VM to the base name
    Then the next GET /images reports that image acquirable

  @AC-41 @TL-1 @TL-2
  Scenario: A broken line keeps the last good list and is reported loudly
    Given a running instance whose catalog is "current" at generation 7
    When the operator introduces a syntax error into "images/macos26/line.conf"
    Then GET /images still lists every image of generation 7
    And its catalog status is "stale" with the failing file, the error and the failure time
    And GET /health reports the catalog status "stale"
    And the service log has exactly one ERROR line for that failure, however many requests follow
    When the operator fixes the file
    Then the next GET /images reports catalog status "current" at a new generation

  @AC-42 @TL-1
  Scenario: No partial catalog is ever published
    Given readers that read the catalog continuously
    When the catalog is rebuilt one thousand times, alternating between two different sets of lines
    Then every snapshot a reader saw is exactly one of the two complete sets, labelled with its own generation and input identity
    And line.conf files were executed only by the process that owns daemon.lock, with the strict parser

  @AC-43 @TL-2 @TL-6
  Scenario: Durable exposure is off unless the operator turns it on
    Given an instance installed without --expose-durable
    Then GET /machines lists no durable machine
    And GET /health reports no "durable" kind
    And an acquisition that names the Mac is refused with HTTP 404 "durable machine not exposed on <instance>"
    And the catalog description it prints has no "durable" tag
    When the operator reinstalls it with --expose-durable on
    Then GET /machines lists the durable machine as "available"

  @AC-46 @TL-1
  Scenario: An installation holds exactly the executables the daemon resolves
    Given a build folder with every executable of the installation layout and one stray file
    When the operator runs "machine-service-install install --prefix DIR" from it into an empty folder
    Then DIR holds exactly the executables of the layout, each byte-equal to its build with mode 0755
    And DIR holds "guest-session-agent" and "guest-session-agent-linux"
    And the LaunchAgent runs DIR's machine-service and ~/.local/bin/machctl links to DIR's machctl
    Given a build folder that lacks any one executable of the layout
    When the operator runs the same installation
    Then it is refused naming that file, and nothing is copied, written or loaded
    Given a Mac without Tart
    When the operator installs with durable exposure on
    Then DIR holds machine-service, machctl and machine-service-install only

  @AC-47 @TL-2 @TL-6
  Scenario: A Mac whose Consul node name is not its own name is listed once, by its own name
    Given a Mac whose LocalHostName is "Mac-mini" and whose Consul node is "mac-mini-m4-pro"
    And the description printed by "machine-service-install catalog-description" is placed there
    Then Consul lists "machine-service" on "mac-mini-m4-pro" with the metadata instance "Mac-mini"
    When the operator runs "machctl list"
    Then the Mac's instance appears once, as "Mac-mini", with its Consul health status
    Given a registration that states no instance
    When the operator runs "machctl list"
    Then that registration is named by its Consul node name
    And standard error says that it states no instance ID and names the command that fixes it

  @AC-48 @TL-2 @TL-6
  Scenario: A Mac with nothing but machctl lists every instance on the network
    Given two instances bound to all interfaces on other Macs, with the default discovery mode
    And this Mac runs no Consul agent and no instance of its own
    When the operator runs "machctl list"
    Then both instances' machines are listed, each under its own instance ID
    And each instance was confirmed by its "/health" before it was listed
    And no request was sent to a Consul agent

  @AC-49 @TL-2
  Scenario: The consul mode stops the advertisement and asks only Consul
    Given an instance started with MACHINE_SERVICE_DISCOVERY set to "consul"
    Then it advertises no "_machine-service._tcp" record
    When the operator runs "machctl list" with MACHINE_SERVICE_DISCOVERY set to "consul"
    Then the CLI asks the Consul agent and browses nothing
    And an advertised instance that Consul does not list is not listed

Feature: Renaming a Mac

  @AC-50 @TL-2
  Scenario: An instance follows a rename without a restart
    Given an instance on a Mac named "Mac-A", advertised on the network
    When the Mac's local host name is changed to "Mac-B"
    Then within 5 seconds a browser sees "Mac-A" removed and "Mac-B" added, with the same machine_id
    And "/health" answers instance "Mac-B" with the same machine_id
    And the daemon's process ID is unchanged

  @AC-51 @TL-2
  Scenario: A held durable lease keeps working through a rename and a restart
    Given a durable lease of "Mac-A" held by a client
    When the Mac is renamed "Mac-B"
    Then exec, push, pull and heartbeat on "Mac-A" with the lease's lease_id succeed
    When the daemon restarts
    Then exec on "Mac-A" with the lease's lease_id still succeeds
    And release of "Mac-A" with the lease's lease_id succeeds
    And afterwards a request for "Mac-A" is refused with 404 naming "Mac-B"

  @AC-52 @TL-2
  Scenario: machctl treats a new name under the same machine_id as a rename
    Given an instance advertised as "Mac-A" whose "/health" answers "Mac-B" with the advertised machine_id
    When the operator runs "machctl list"
    Then the instance is listed once, as "Mac-B"
    Given an instance whose "/health" answers a different machine_id than it advertised
    When the operator runs "machctl list"
    Then it is listed as unreachable with the two machine IDs

  @AC-53 @TL-2
  Scenario: A command during the gap between the goodbye and the new advertisement still succeeds
    Given a durable lease of "Mac-A" remembered by machctl
    And the Mac is renamed "Mac-B" so that its new advertisement arrives 1 second after the goodbye
    When the operator runs "machctl exec Mac-A -- true" in that second
    Then the command succeeds on the second look

  @AC-54 @TL-2
  Scenario: The Consul description never goes stale
    Given an instance installed with MACHINE_SERVICE_DISCOVERY set to "consul"
    Then its service-catalog description states machine_id and no instance name
    When the Mac is renamed
    Then a client in consul mode confirms the instance by machine_id and lists it under its new name
    And nothing was reinstalled
